[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
OpenSearch Dashboards 2.17.1 runs here on the Node.js 18 of the package node18
(the Node.js line of 2.17.1); node18 and node24 cannot be installed together, so
this package and kibana6 (on node24) do not go on one server.

There is no security plugin (%%OSD_PLUGINS_OUT%%) in this package: OpenSearch
Dashboards talks to OpenSearch over plain http without credentials
(opensearch.hosts, default http://localhost:9200; Node.js 18 connects to the
first address the system gives for localhost and tries no other, ::1 on a host
with IPv6, so OpenSearch has to listen there too, as its default network.host
does, or write 127.0.0.1). The rc script refuses to start with a setting of that
plugin in %%ETCDIR%%/opensearch_dashboards.yml (%%OSD_CONFIG_OUT%%):
OpenSearch Dashboards would stop at its start on it. Without the security plugin
everyone who reaches its port can do everything: keep it behind a firewall or a
proxy with authentication.

The options of Node.js (--max-old-space-size and the like) go into
%%ETCDIR%%/node.options, one per line. Its log is rolled at 10 MB without
archives by newsyslog (%%PREFIX%%/etc/newsyslog.conf.d/opensearch_dashboards.conf);
service opensearch-dashboards reload opens it again. Its tools
(bin/opensearch-dashboards-plugin and -keystore in %%WWWDIR%%) stop as root
without --allow-root, as upstream.

Stop the service before this package replaces the official one: this rc script
keeps its pid file in /var/run/opensearch_dashboards/, the official one in
/var/run/opensearch_dashboards.pid (if that one still runs:
kill `cat /var/run/opensearch_dashboards.pid`).
EOM
}
]
